{"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"]},{"title":"Explanation","generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Design Principles","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"type":"text","text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" generates that class for you ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<StructName>Observer"},{"type":"text","text":") and wires up the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe"},{"type":"text","text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous","text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers take "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"type":"text","text":" and an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":". They never "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":", never "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"throw"},{"type":"text","text":", and never call I\/O directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a "},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"code":"send","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" runs effects in "},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so they don’t block UI. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state."}]},{"text":"4. Persistence is invisible","anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers mutate "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" properties; "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" records every change in a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" debounces and drains those changesets through "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You never write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two structural patterns:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Core middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape ("},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for undo; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" keypaths for persistence).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain plugins","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does this need to know your action type?"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write core middleware and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to "},{"code":"Binding(get:set:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and write back on a button."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", those plugins are blind to it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The recommended order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","type":"heading","text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)"},{"text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@concurrent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async\/await"},{"type":"text","text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux gives you a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppEnvironment"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A network layer (use "},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" and Swidux doesn’t care)."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Anti-patterns","type":"heading","text":"Anti-patterns"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"try","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" from inside a reducer — use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Owning the store with "},{"code":"@StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObservableObject"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Buffering form state in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Registering "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" before "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — snapshot must precede mutation."}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","title":"ChangeSet"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"title":"Send","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","abstract":[{"text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","title":"PersistencePlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"title":"binding(_:sending:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that reads a property through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"binding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC","text":"KeyPath","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa","text":"Observer","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sending","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV","text":"Binding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"title":"Effect","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"title":"StateWriter","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","abstract":[{"text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"title":"EntityStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","title":"Build Your First Swidux App"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","title":"UndoPlugin"}}}